1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:05,880
<i>I see.</i>

2
00:00:05,964 --> 00:00:07,257
<i>Orange peels…</i>

3
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:10,010
<i>-If you want, we can make them together.</i>
<i>-No, I can't do it.</i>

4
00:00:10,093 --> 00:00:11,428
<i>You can!</i>

5
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:15,015
<i>I'm glad I met you, Mr. Nishigami.</i>

6
00:00:15,098 --> 00:00:17,058
You're interested in Midori, aren't you?

7
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:18,977
<i>But she probably…</i>

8
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,979
<i>Do you think we can be a couple?</i>

9
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:25,358
"A woman's heart
is a deep ocean of secrets."

10
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:27,110
<i>Mr. Nishigami…</i>

11
00:00:27,193 --> 00:00:29,112
<i>Do you have a girlfriend?</i>

12
00:00:29,195 --> 00:00:31,781
No. I have no one like that.

13
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:34,868
I may be falling in love
for the first time!

14
00:00:35,702 --> 00:00:39,080
<i>You're getting friendly again</i>
<i>with those people.</i>

15
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:39,998
<i>Given your position,</i>

16
00:00:40,081 --> 00:00:43,084
<i>falling in love with a human</i>
<i>is out of the question.</i>

17
00:00:43,168 --> 00:00:45,587
Be careful on your way home.
See you tomorrow.

18
00:00:47,046 --> 00:00:48,256
See you tomorrow.

19
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:54,054
TWO DAYS LATER

20
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:18,161
Veggies first.

21
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:19,621
Yeah, veggies first.

22
00:01:19,704 --> 00:01:21,039
-Is this crab paste?
-Yummy.

23
00:01:21,122 --> 00:01:22,290
-It's good.
-Crab paste?

24
00:01:22,373 --> 00:01:24,167
-Oh, this is crab paste.
-Really?

25
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:26,044
It's crab paste.

26
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:27,170
-Try it.
-I will.

27
00:01:27,253 --> 00:01:28,630
It's like regular mayonnaise.

28
00:01:28,713 --> 00:01:30,465
Really? It tastes like crab paste.

29
00:01:31,007 --> 00:01:32,258
Yeah, it's crab paste.

30
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:34,260
-It is.
-Thank you for the meal.

31
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:36,805
Oh, it's fine. Leave it there.

32
00:01:36,888 --> 00:01:37,847
I'll wash it.

33
00:01:37,931 --> 00:01:39,015
Thank you.

34
00:01:39,098 --> 00:01:40,016
Good night.

35
00:01:40,099 --> 00:01:41,768
Good night!

36
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:46,856
I wonder what happened to Midori?

37
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:48,942
She's been down these past two days.

38
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:50,527
Did she get sick or something?

39
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:52,195
Huh? I didn't notice at all.

40
00:01:52,862 --> 00:01:54,989
Konta, how dense can you be?

41
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:56,866
What? Did something happen to her?

42
00:01:57,992 --> 00:01:59,828
-Right?
-Yeah.

43
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:01,287
What is it?

44
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:04,541
She's probably down because
Mr. Nishigami hasn't been coming.

45
00:02:05,291 --> 00:02:06,209
What?

46
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:11,256
Hey, Midori, seriously?

47
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:12,382
Is that how it is?

48
00:02:13,091 --> 00:02:15,301
So she…

49
00:02:16,803 --> 00:02:18,221
and Mr. Nishigami?

50
00:02:18,888 --> 00:02:19,973
Are they…

51
00:02:20,056 --> 00:02:21,307
a couple yet?

52
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:23,601
It's finally here.

53
00:02:23,685 --> 00:02:25,770
Midori's first love.

54
00:02:25,854 --> 00:02:27,480
That's certainly what it is.

55
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:30,942
Still, Mr. Nishigami hasn't come
for the past two days.

56
00:02:31,025 --> 00:02:32,610
Why is that? Why isn't he coming?

57
00:02:32,694 --> 00:02:34,028
No idea, seriously.

58
00:02:34,112 --> 00:02:36,197
-He used to come almost every day.
-Right?

59
00:02:36,281 --> 00:02:38,283
Hey, the last time he came,

60
00:02:38,366 --> 00:02:40,869
he and Midori were making
orange peels together, right?

61
00:02:40,952 --> 00:02:42,245
Did something happen then?

62
00:02:42,328 --> 00:02:44,372
They were having fun!
Which is why it's strange.

63
00:02:44,455 --> 00:02:47,917
Right? So what's up with Mr. Nishigami?

64
00:02:48,001 --> 00:02:50,545
He isn't playing
with Midori's feelings, right?

65
00:02:50,628 --> 00:02:53,673
Well, I wonder.

66
00:02:53,756 --> 00:02:54,883
What should we do?

67
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:56,885
I mean, is Midori even aware of it?

68
00:02:56,968 --> 00:02:58,595
Of her own love.

69
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:00,722
No idea.

70
00:03:00,805 --> 00:03:02,682
She's the sister of that idiot, after all.

71
00:03:02,765 --> 00:03:03,892
Idiot?

72
00:03:03,975 --> 00:03:05,977
Konta is an idiot, but a cute one!

73
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:08,813
Sure. And are you hooking up
with that idiot?

74
00:03:08,897 --> 00:03:10,940
Nope. We're not dating yet.

75
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:12,692
Right now, I'm making him chase me.

76
00:03:14,485 --> 00:03:16,738
Well, whatever.
Right now, it's about Midori.

77
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:17,697
What do we do?

78
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:20,116
But, you know Midori's personality.

79
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:23,786
If we say something like,
"You like Mr. Nishigami, don't you?"

80
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:25,330
She won't admit it.

81
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:27,040
Well, yeah.

82
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:30,126
Her dating experience
is like a middle schooler's.

83
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:32,754
For now, let's wait and see.

84
00:03:32,837 --> 00:03:34,756
Tetsuro needs to do his best.

85
00:03:34,839 --> 00:03:36,216
Huh, Tetsuro?

86
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:37,842
Why is he relevant here?

87
00:03:37,926 --> 00:03:40,220
That guy is crazy about Midori.

88
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:41,262
What?

89
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:45,141
It seems he hasn't even realized
his own feelings, though.

90
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:48,311
We have too many love novices here.

91
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:49,896
It makes me laugh.

92
00:03:49,979 --> 00:03:53,942
Spoken like an expert.
A girl with a clingy ex.

93
00:03:54,734 --> 00:03:55,777
What?

94
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:57,028
How did you know that?

95
00:03:57,111 --> 00:04:00,490
Your ex looked
at your social media followers,

96
00:04:00,573 --> 00:04:02,700
found me, and sent me a message.

97
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:06,663
He said, "I want to get back
with Tsumugi, so please persuade her."

98
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:08,581
How gross!

99
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:13,294
I'm sure he saw photos and videos
of you having fun at this villa,

100
00:04:13,378 --> 00:04:16,005
so he wants to have fun with you again.

101
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:20,260
Well, it's true that
back when I was with him,

102
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:23,263
before coming here, I didn't smile much.

103
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:24,180
Yeah.

104
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:27,058
Since coming to this villa,
I think you look prettier.

105
00:04:27,141 --> 00:04:28,643
-Huh, seriously?
-Yeah.

106
00:04:29,143 --> 00:04:30,895
Maybe it's the vitamin from the oranges?

107
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:35,149
Well, that's part of it, but when
you're surrounded by nature like this

108
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:36,734
and doing fun things,

109
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:40,738
your mind, body,
and your appearance are all healed.

110
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:43,157
That's the ultimate beauty method.

111
00:04:43,241 --> 00:04:44,075
Right.

112
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:48,246
Even without money,
you can become beautiful.

113
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:53,501
Mr. Nishigami…

114
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:56,671
You said, "See you tomorrow"…

115
00:05:01,884 --> 00:05:04,012
The orange peels are also ready.

116
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:25,283
Midori, what are you doing?

117
00:05:26,367 --> 00:05:27,660
I'm going out for a bit.

118
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:28,578
Going where?

119
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:32,749
To Mr. Nishigami's place.
We made these, after all.

120
00:05:32,832 --> 00:05:34,500
Do you know where he lives?

121
00:05:35,084 --> 00:05:36,294
I don't…

122
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:37,837
But,

123
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:41,591
I will absolutely make him eat these.

124
00:06:53,454 --> 00:06:54,413
Hey.

125
00:06:56,374 --> 00:06:57,792
How are you doing?

126
00:06:57,875 --> 00:07:00,002
Mountain God, Sea God.

127
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:01,963
-Hello.
-What's up?

128
00:07:02,713 --> 00:07:03,881
You look gloomy.

129
00:07:07,051 --> 00:07:08,136
Could it be…

130
00:07:08,219 --> 00:07:09,512
You got scolded by our boss?

131
00:07:10,513 --> 00:07:11,848
Sorry.

132
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:16,811
During some small talk
I may have told them everything.

133
00:07:17,395 --> 00:07:18,604
It's fine.

134
00:07:18,688 --> 00:07:20,440
I'm the one at fault here.

135
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:25,570
We're worried about you too.

136
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:28,239
You're a Grim Reaper.

137
00:07:28,322 --> 00:07:32,410
A Reaper's job is to bear witness
to destined deaths, right?

138
00:07:33,619 --> 00:07:37,081
So, if you get too involved
with humans, things get…

139
00:07:37,165 --> 00:07:38,166
You know.

140
00:07:39,208 --> 00:07:40,126
I…

141
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:41,836
understand that.

142
00:07:43,671 --> 00:07:44,755
What's wrong?

143
00:07:45,423 --> 00:07:47,717
-Grim Reaper--
-Mr. Nishigami!

144
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:52,889
What's with you?

145
00:07:53,431 --> 00:07:54,932
Huh, what?

146
00:07:55,016 --> 00:07:55,933
What's wrong?

147
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:57,935
She's cute. Huh? What's going on?

148
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:00,563
Is she the reason?

149
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:05,485
Mr. Nishigami,
you're avoiding me, aren't you?

150
00:08:06,068 --> 00:08:07,195
I am not.

151
00:08:07,278 --> 00:08:09,238
You are!

152
00:08:11,365 --> 00:08:12,200
Here.

153
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:14,285
The orange peels we made together.

154
00:08:15,119 --> 00:08:17,830
You stopped coming over,
so I brought them.

155
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:20,208
They turned out delicious.

156
00:08:20,708 --> 00:08:21,751
Here.

157
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:24,504
I don't want them.

158
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:25,421
What?

159
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:26,756
I'm sorry.

160
00:08:27,298 --> 00:08:28,216
I don't want them.

161
00:08:28,716 --> 00:08:30,092
Seriously?

162
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:31,928
What is that supposed to mean?

163
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:37,266
I thought we had finally become close.

164
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:39,769
So it was all my misunderstanding?

165
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:40,811
Fine then.

166
00:08:41,479 --> 00:08:42,355
I'll just…

167
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:44,690
feed these to the fish.

168
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:06,439
Mr. Nishigami!

169
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:12,862
Thank you very much.
For the shower and clothes.

170
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:14,739
Never mind that.

171
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:18,117
Mr. Nishigami, what's the matter?

172
00:10:18,701 --> 00:10:20,578
You suddenly jumped into the sea.

173
00:10:21,162 --> 00:10:22,121
But…

174
00:10:22,788 --> 00:10:24,206
The orange peels…

175
00:10:30,588 --> 00:10:31,756
Please sit down.

176
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:34,425
Excuse me.

177
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:42,767
Go ahead.

178
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:45,978
Thank you.

179
00:10:57,281 --> 00:10:58,699
It's very delicious.

180
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:02,870
I'm glad.

181
00:11:13,923 --> 00:11:15,174
Mr. Nishigami…

182
00:11:17,468 --> 00:11:21,472
You haven't come by here
for the past two days.

183
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:24,016
Could it be…

184
00:11:26,435 --> 00:11:29,438
you have come to dislike us?

185
00:11:30,898 --> 00:11:33,025
It's not that.

186
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:42,243
Then, please come again!
You can come anytime.

187
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:44,161
I…

188
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:46,122
Mr. Nishigami…

189
00:11:46,622 --> 00:11:48,666
I'm home.

190
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:50,459
Welcome back.

191
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,211
Oh, Mr. Nishigami!

192
00:11:52,294 --> 00:11:53,587
Long time no see.

193
00:11:53,671 --> 00:11:55,423
Why are you in my clothes?

194
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:56,882
Oh, things happened.

195
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:58,008
Let him borrow them.

196
00:11:58,092 --> 00:11:59,093
Sure, totally fine.

197
00:11:59,176 --> 00:12:00,970
Mr. Nishigami, this is perfect timing.

198
00:12:01,053 --> 00:12:02,555
We're doing a barbecue today too.

199
00:12:02,638 --> 00:12:04,265
Would you like to join us?

200
00:12:05,599 --> 00:12:06,559
I'll help.

201
00:12:22,908 --> 00:12:24,034
Mr. Nishigami!

202
00:12:25,995 --> 00:12:28,747
I want you to tell me honestly.

203
00:12:29,373 --> 00:12:32,001
How do you feel about Midori?

204
00:12:32,084 --> 00:12:33,002
What?

205
00:12:34,044 --> 00:12:37,465
You see, you're handsome,
so I think you're popular.

206
00:12:37,548 --> 00:12:40,676
But Midori is completely
unused to romance.

207
00:12:40,759 --> 00:12:43,220
That's right, unlike us.

208
00:12:44,013 --> 00:12:46,182
All right!

209
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:48,726
All the ingredients are here.

210
00:12:48,809 --> 00:12:52,313
Let us barbecue pros get things going!

211
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:54,356
Barbecue pros?

212
00:12:55,024 --> 00:12:57,485
It has been a whole month
since we came to this villa.

213
00:12:57,568 --> 00:13:00,529
We are practically vacation pros now.

214
00:13:00,613 --> 00:13:03,741
So, to celebrate our vacation so far,

215
00:13:04,408 --> 00:13:08,829
I would like to hold
the ultimate barbecue!

216
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:14,585
Rinrin, you've become
really good at cooking.

217
00:13:14,668 --> 00:13:15,628
That's right.

218
00:13:15,711 --> 00:13:18,714
Before I came here,
I wouldn't even touch raw fish.

219
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:22,676
-You've grown during the vacation.
-Yeah.

220
00:13:24,762 --> 00:13:26,680
Let's see what we've got.

221
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:29,683
Oh, it's raw squid.

222
00:13:29,767 --> 00:13:31,519
What are you doing with this?

223
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:32,937
The squid…

224
00:13:33,854 --> 00:13:34,813
I will marinate it!

225
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:36,065
Oh, nice.

226
00:13:36,148 --> 00:13:38,651
-That sounds good.
-We should have wine today.

227
00:13:38,734 --> 00:13:40,736
That works.

228
00:13:42,446 --> 00:13:45,741
Should we use red or white wine?

229
00:13:45,824 --> 00:13:48,744
-Maybe white.
-White wine.

230
00:13:50,496 --> 00:13:53,207
Take a look at it! It's so slimy.

231
00:13:53,290 --> 00:13:55,626
Oh, nice. Liver is tasty too.

232
00:13:55,709 --> 00:13:57,044
Nice.

233
00:13:57,127 --> 00:13:58,712
Oh, wow.

234
00:13:58,796 --> 00:14:00,256
It must feel good.

235
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:03,384
All right.

236
00:14:04,301 --> 00:14:05,219
Let's marinate!

237
00:14:05,302 --> 00:14:06,679
Mr. Nishigami, watch closely.

238
00:14:06,762 --> 00:14:07,930
Here goes.

239
00:14:08,013 --> 00:14:09,306
Oh, my shirt suits you!

240
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:11,058
-Thank you.
-A bit small?

241
00:14:11,141 --> 00:14:12,726
You're too ripped.

242
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:15,604
Let's do this.

243
00:14:37,626 --> 00:14:38,627
Hey.

244
00:14:39,503 --> 00:14:42,006
About you and Midori…

245
00:14:45,384 --> 00:14:48,012
The AI said I'm in love with her.

246
00:14:48,095 --> 00:14:49,013
I knew it.

247
00:14:49,638 --> 00:14:50,723
Really?

248
00:14:50,806 --> 00:14:56,228
It seems that, because of this vacation,
it's now easier for us to fall in love.

249
00:14:56,854 --> 00:15:02,401
So, my feelings
are just the memories of this summer.

250
00:15:03,944 --> 00:15:06,155
But I surprised myself too.

251
00:15:06,822 --> 00:15:09,158
To think that I would fall in love.

252
00:15:10,159 --> 00:15:14,413
Being able to experience this feeling
made coming here worth it.

253
00:15:15,789 --> 00:15:18,876
Then, why not make a move on Midori?

254
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:24,840
Midori probably likes Mr. Nishigami.

255
00:15:25,799 --> 00:15:29,970
And, Mr. Nishigami is my barbecue master…

256
00:15:31,221 --> 00:15:33,682
So, I want

257
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:36,977
the two of them to be happy.

258
00:15:37,061 --> 00:15:38,896
-You're supporting them as a couple?
-Yes.

259
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,898
A new form of love, huh.

260
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:45,861
All right, should be enough.

261
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:47,112
How about you guys?

262
00:15:47,696 --> 00:15:48,781
-Doing good.
-Great.

263
00:15:48,864 --> 00:15:50,115
Okay.

264
00:15:51,116 --> 00:15:52,952
-Good.
-Here?

265
00:15:53,035 --> 00:15:55,037
-Right.
-Perfect.

266
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:57,164
-Wait, I haven't spun this enough.
-Huh?

267
00:15:57,247 --> 00:15:59,708
If you need to light it, shall I help?

268
00:15:59,792 --> 00:16:01,585
It's fine. I got this.

269
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:09,718
Nice!

270
00:16:09,802 --> 00:16:11,220
It's lit!

271
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:15,182
-There it goes!
-Look at you all…

272
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:20,396
Compared to when you first came here,
you feel like different people now.

273
00:16:20,479 --> 00:16:21,605
Well, yeah.

274
00:16:21,689 --> 00:16:23,399
Stay back a bit.

275
00:16:23,482 --> 00:16:25,150
Watch out.

276
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:26,318
-Well then!
-Well then!

277
00:16:26,402 --> 00:16:27,820
Well then!

278
00:16:27,903 --> 00:16:30,656
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

279
00:16:31,865 --> 00:16:33,117
So good!

280
00:16:33,784 --> 00:16:34,743
It's delicious.

281
00:16:34,827 --> 00:16:37,913
Right? I made it with summer oranges,
white wine and soda.

282
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:40,332
You didn't put lemon sour mix
or gum syrup in it, right?

283
00:16:40,416 --> 00:16:41,583
I didn't!

284
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:43,669
I stopped making it.
The hangovers were crazy.

285
00:16:43,752 --> 00:16:46,088
-Right?
-I never want to be hungover again!

286
00:16:46,171 --> 00:16:49,049
When you're a vacation newbie,
you tend to get overexcited, huh.

287
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:51,135
Exactly. Konta, is it done?

288
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:53,554
-A bit more… Oh, no, it's done!
-We can eat now?

289
00:16:53,637 --> 00:16:56,056
-Okay.
-Mr. Nishigami, drink with us.

290
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:59,476
-Here you go.
-Thanks.

291
00:17:06,734 --> 00:17:07,901
It's delicious.

292
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:09,319
It's like…

293
00:17:09,403 --> 00:17:11,155
Huh? What is it?

294
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:14,992
No, I was just thinking,
a handsome guy looks good just drinking.

295
00:17:15,075 --> 00:17:17,661
Yeah. I can drink to that view.

296
00:17:17,745 --> 00:17:20,414
Hey, you two are making him uncomfortable!

297
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:22,082
Right?

298
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:27,004
Then Midori, you don't find him handsome?

299
00:17:27,671 --> 00:17:29,506
That's not true, but…

300
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:31,258
Oh, so you do think so.

301
00:17:31,341 --> 00:17:32,843
You think he's handsome.

302
00:17:34,261 --> 00:17:35,596
Well, yeah…

303
00:17:38,098 --> 00:17:39,016
What is this?

304
00:17:39,099 --> 00:17:40,517
Mr. Nishigami.

305
00:17:40,601 --> 00:17:42,478
You're quite a playboy, huh?

306
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:43,687
-Hey, cut it out!
-Konta!

307
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:46,106
Stop it! Why are you moving like that?

308
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:47,816
Cut it out! Eat up!

309
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,234
-Everyone.
-Huh?

310
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:50,986
We have carpaccio and marinated dishes.

311
00:17:54,406 --> 00:17:56,241
I'm gonna drink too much
and get a hangover.

312
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:57,785
I can see that.

313
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:00,204
-Oh, Rinrin.
-Yes?

314
00:18:00,287 --> 00:18:02,581
-You want this? <i>Ajillo</i>.
-A tomato?

315
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:05,084
I'll feed you some!

316
00:18:06,710 --> 00:18:08,253
-Yummy!
-Is it?

317
00:18:10,547 --> 00:18:13,217
I don't want to go back to Tokyo anymore.

318
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:14,134
Me neither.

319
00:18:14,218 --> 00:18:16,386
Then, shall we all just live here?

320
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:19,098
Maybe I should move my address here.

321
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:24,186
I'll work part-time at a supermarket here
and earn the bare minimum.

322
00:18:24,269 --> 00:18:26,897
-Nice.
-That's awesome. Maybe I'll try farming.

323
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:30,109
Cooking with vegetables I grew myself.
Isn't that the best?

324
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:31,151
Yeah!

325
00:18:31,235 --> 00:18:35,781
Maybe I'll look for a remote job too.
Oh, let's install high-capacity Wi-Fi.

326
00:18:35,864 --> 00:18:37,241
Then, we can work online.

327
00:18:37,324 --> 00:18:39,493
I'll only go back to Tokyo for work.

328
00:18:39,576 --> 00:18:41,495
Otherwise, I'll just live here and drink.

329
00:18:41,578 --> 00:18:44,164
If I help out the lady next door,
I can earn 5,000 yen.

330
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:47,251
I also got hooked on fishing,
so maybe I'll keep living here.

331
00:18:48,001 --> 00:18:50,629
I think since COVID,
more people have been living like this

332
00:18:50,712 --> 00:18:52,047
while working remotely.

333
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:53,090
Yeah.

334
00:18:55,592 --> 00:18:56,802
Mr. Nishigami?

335
00:19:00,097 --> 00:19:00,931
It's nothing.

336
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:03,851
Want some meat?

337
00:19:03,934 --> 00:19:05,060
I've just grilled some.

338
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:06,061
Here you go.

339
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:11,942
Here's the meat marinated in sauce
made from our usual summer oranges.

340
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:12,943
Looks so good.

341
00:19:13,026 --> 00:19:14,111
Here you go.

342
00:19:14,194 --> 00:19:16,155
-Dig in.
-Thank you for the food.

343
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:21,702
-Here.
-Thanks.

344
00:19:24,413 --> 00:19:26,748
-Hot.
-Oh, no! Are you okay?

345
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:33,797
It's delicious.

346
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:35,757
I'm glad.

347
00:19:39,344 --> 00:19:40,637
-Eat up, everyone.
-Yeah.

348
00:19:44,641 --> 00:19:49,897
This is what they call "chilling."

349
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:54,568
This is so chill, yeah.

350
00:19:54,651 --> 00:19:56,361
-You get hooked on this.
-Yeah.

351
00:19:56,987 --> 00:19:59,198
Now I see why people go camping.

352
00:19:59,781 --> 00:20:03,243
But, you know, at campsites,
you have strangers nearby.

353
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:05,662
There's no one here.
This place is the best.

354
00:20:05,746 --> 00:20:08,665
True. I love villas!

355
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:13,837
You know, I saw a street interview on TV
before, and a foreigner said,

356
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:16,673
"Japanese people can't enjoy vacations."

357
00:20:17,257 --> 00:20:21,011
But aren't we
enjoying a perfect vacation now?

358
00:20:21,094 --> 00:20:24,640
Thanks to Mr. Nishigami,
our vacation skills have improved a lot.

359
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:26,767
What?

360
00:20:27,434 --> 00:20:31,271
Thanks to you and this villa,
all of us have grown.

361
00:20:32,481 --> 00:20:34,274
I didn't do anything.

362
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:37,653
At first, I only came here
to run away from reality,

363
00:20:37,736 --> 00:20:41,657
but you taught us
many things and helped us.

364
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:45,160
So we've had a fun and safe vacation.

365
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:48,038
Thank you for always protecting the villa.

366
00:20:49,081 --> 00:20:50,123
Keep up the good work!

367
00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:51,959
We're counting on you, Nishiyan.

368
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:53,043
Nishiyan?

369
00:20:53,126 --> 00:20:54,211
What's with that nickname?

370
00:20:54,294 --> 00:20:56,546
He is our vacation master, after all.

371
00:20:56,630 --> 00:20:58,757
That's true. Master Nishiyan.

372
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:00,217
Thank you, Nishiyan.

373
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:01,468
Nishiyan.

374
00:21:04,721 --> 00:21:06,640
-Let's take a photo.
-So suddenly?

375
00:21:06,723 --> 00:21:08,016
This is the perfect time!

376
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:09,685
Let's capture
the best moment of our lives!

377
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:11,561
-True.
-Oh, then…

378
00:21:11,645 --> 00:21:13,146
-Huh?
-I'll take it for you.

379
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:15,941
What are you saying? You've got
to be in the photo too, Nishiyan!

380
00:21:16,024 --> 00:21:17,484
Look, there's a timer.

381
00:21:17,567 --> 00:21:19,903
Wow, your hands are thick and manly.

382
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:21,655
Let's go, come on.

383
00:21:21,738 --> 00:21:23,573
-All right!
-There's a timer!

384
00:21:23,657 --> 00:21:25,200
-See, a timer!
-Come join us.

385
00:21:25,284 --> 00:21:28,287
-Okay. It's set for ten seconds.
-Okay!

386
00:21:28,370 --> 00:21:29,788
-You good?
-I pressed it.

387
00:21:29,871 --> 00:21:32,207
-Oops!
-What are you doing?

388
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:35,377
Six, five, four…

389
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:36,503
Three.

390
00:21:36,586 --> 00:21:37,421
Two.

391
00:21:37,504 --> 00:21:38,338
One.

392
00:21:41,591 --> 00:21:42,759
<i>Mr. Nishigami.</i>

393
00:21:42,843 --> 00:21:44,261
This is for you.

394
00:21:46,096 --> 00:21:47,055
I'm good…

395
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:50,892
We can print more for ourselves.

396
00:21:50,976 --> 00:21:52,686
You should have this.

397
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:56,231
May I?

398
00:21:56,898 --> 00:21:57,983
Of course.

399
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:13,582
<i>A typhoon is coming soon.</i>

400
00:22:13,665 --> 00:22:17,711
<i>Because of it, a landslide will occur,</i>
<i>and that villa will be destroyed.</i>

401
00:22:18,378 --> 00:22:22,341
<i>Those five you are</i>
<i>so close with will all die.</i>

402
00:22:30,223 --> 00:22:31,349
Mr. Nishigami.

403
00:22:31,975 --> 00:22:32,934
What's wrong?

404
00:22:36,563 --> 00:22:37,522
I'm fine.

405
00:22:38,231 --> 00:22:39,232
It's nothing.

406
00:22:40,525 --> 00:22:41,568
It's nothing.

407
00:23:09,971 --> 00:23:12,557
This typhoon is quite strong, huh.

408
00:23:12,641 --> 00:23:14,101
It will probably miss us.

409
00:23:14,184 --> 00:23:16,228
<i>Will Mr. Nishigami come?</i>

410
00:23:16,311 --> 00:23:17,395
It will be fine!

411
00:23:17,479 --> 00:23:19,314
<i>It's not raining that much yet.</i>

412
00:23:27,739 --> 00:23:29,324
Looks like a fun time, huh?

413
00:23:29,908 --> 00:23:30,826
Now…

414
00:23:30,909 --> 00:23:32,702
This is your final warning.

415
00:23:33,662 --> 00:23:34,663
<i>Mr. Nishigami?</i>

416
00:23:35,247 --> 00:23:36,581
Such a thing is impossible!

417
00:23:36,665 --> 00:23:38,250
Listen up, Reaper.

418
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:41,086
You'll be erased like sand by Lady Yomi.

419
00:23:41,670 --> 00:23:44,131
<i>Don't forget. You are a Grim Reaper.</i>

420
00:23:45,048 --> 00:23:46,007
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
